# Component Design Principles

This document outlines the core design principles and styling guidelines for our UI components. These principles ensure consistency across all integration components while maintaining a clean, modern aesthetic.

## Card Components

Cards are fundamental building blocks of our UI. They display concise information about entities in a consistent format.

### Standard Card Structure

1. **Layout**:
   - Cards display two per row by default
   - Minimum width: 250px
   - Responsive: Cards stack on smaller screens

2. **Content Structure**:
   - Left side: Icon + Title + Subtitle
   - Right side: Entity representation (status, avatar, tags, etc.)

3. **Title Section**:
   - Small icon/link icon on the left (optional)
   - Title text (bold, truncated with ellipsis if too long)
   - External link icon (if applicable)

4. **Subtitle Section**:
   - Up to 3 pieces of information
   - Separated by middot character (·)
   - Examples: assignee, status, priority, date

5. **Right Section Options**:
   - Status badge
   - User avatar
   - Tags collection
   - Action button

